  "live_records": {
    "q-251875": {
      "dom_id": "step-q251875",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $5$ | $8$ | $9$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xy}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overset{―}{x}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{5+8+9+5+6}{5}=6.6\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{8+9+10+7+9}{5}=8.6\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $5$ | $8$ | $9$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $-1.6$ | $1.4$ | $2.4$ | $-1.6$ | $-0.6$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1.4$ | $-1.6$ | $0.4$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $0.96$ | $0.56$ | $3.36$ | $2.56$ | $-0.24$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=0.96+0.56+3.36+2.56+(-0.24)=7.2.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
