    "q-251876": {
      "dom_id": "step-q251876",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the two sets of $7$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $1.2$ | $1.0$ | $0.7$ | $1.3$ | $1.8$ | $1.7$ | $1.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $6.6$ | $6.1$ | $5.7$ | $6.0$ | $6.3$ | $5.9$ | $5.4$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xy}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overset{―}{x}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1.2+1.0+0.7+1.3+1.8+1.4+1.7}{7}=1.3\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{6.6+6.1+5.7+6.0+6.3+5.9+5.4}{7}=6\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $1.2$ | $1.0$ | $0.7$ | $1.3$ | $1.8$ | $1.7$ | $1.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $6.6$ | $6.1$ | $5.7$ | $6.0$ | $6.3$ | $5.9$ | $5.4$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $-0.1$ | $-0.3$ | $-0.6$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $0.6$ | $0.1$ | $-0.3$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $-0.1$ | $-0.6$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-0.06$ | $-0.03$ | $0.18$ | $0$ | $0.15$ | $-0.04$ | $-0.06$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=(-0.06)+(-0.03)+0.18+0+0.15+(-0.04)+(-0.06)=0.14.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
